// trap: .on_delete(set_null) keeps its one-row delete, with no guard and no DanglingKey rule.
// The key is optional: AddLine creates an unlinked line, and Attach links it to an Order.
// The lifecycle does not null the key when the Order goes, and no guard waits for the
// lines, since the database would unlink them. CancelDraft marks the line it binds, which
// the Order's key names, as orphaned in the same step, so the line is left present and
// orphaned after Open, AddLine, Attach, CancelDraft, and Forbidden_OrderLine_0 fails. The
// key gets no DanglingKey_* rule: the engine does not run the set_null, and the warning
// DeleteLeavesChildKeys names CancelDraft. An engine that put
// the restrict guard on a set_null key would never run CancelDraft while the line names the
// Order and would answer ok. BFS refutes the rule, so the proof does not try it;
// proof_equivalence checks that z3 would not prove it.
// expect Forbidden_OrderLine_0: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample z3=refuted
entity Order "注文" { id: Int @pk }
entity OrderLine "明細" { id: Int @pk  orphaned: Bool @default(false) }
relate(OrderLine, Order, N:1).optional().on_delete(set_null)
usecase Open "起票"
usecase AddLine "明細追加"
usecase Attach "紐付け"
usecase CancelDraft "下書き取消"
creates(Open, Order)
creates(AddLine, OrderLine)
links(Attach, OrderLine, Order)
deletes(CancelDraft, Order)
sets(CancelDraft, OrderLine.orphaned == true)
forbidden(OrderLine, OrderLine.orphaned == true)
